   <refbody>    <section>
      <p>Consider a "backup Command" chapter in a "CLI Reference Guide" document where you want to document command syntax, options, variables, keywords, and command output. Instead of documenting commands as plain text, use CLI-specific DITA elements to describe the command structure semantically.</p>
      <codeblock xml:space="preserve">&lt;reference id="backup-command"&gt;
&lt;title&gt;backup Command&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;shortdesc&gt;
Creates a backup of application data and configuration files.
&lt;/shortdesc&gt;
&lt;refbody&gt;
&lt;section&gt;
&lt;title&gt;Command Syntax&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
&lt;synph&gt;
&lt;cmdname&gt;backup&lt;/cmdname&gt;
&lt;option&gt;--full&lt;/option&gt;
&lt;option&gt;--compress&lt;/option&gt;
&lt;var&gt;destination&lt;/var&gt;
&lt;/synph&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section&gt;
&lt;title&gt;Syntax Diagram&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;syntaxdiagram&gt;
&lt;groupseq&gt;
&lt;cmdname&gt;backup&lt;/cmdname&gt;
&lt;groupchoice&gt;
&lt;option&gt;--full&lt;/option&gt;
&lt;option&gt;--incremental&lt;/option&gt;
&lt;/groupchoice&gt;
&lt;option&gt;--compress&lt;/option&gt;
&lt;var&gt;destination&lt;/var&gt;
&lt;/groupseq&gt;
&lt;/syntaxdiagram&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section&gt;
&lt;title&gt;Syntax Components&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;simpletable relcolwidth="1* 2*"&gt;
&lt;sthead&gt;
&lt;stentry&gt;Element&lt;/stentry&gt;
&lt;stentry&gt;Description&lt;/stentry&gt;
&lt;/sthead&gt;
&lt;strow&gt;
&lt;stentry&gt;
&lt;cmdname&gt;backup&lt;/cmdname&gt;
&lt;/stentry&gt;
&lt;stentry&gt;
Executable command name.
&lt;/stentry&gt;
&lt;/strow&gt;
&lt;strow&gt;
&lt;stentry&gt;
&lt;option&gt;--full&lt;/option&gt;
&lt;/stentry&gt;
&lt;stentry&gt;
Creates a complete backup.
&lt;/stentry&gt;
&lt;/strow&gt;
&lt;strow&gt;
&lt;stentry&gt;
&lt;var&gt;destination&lt;/var&gt;
&lt;/stentry&gt;
&lt;stentry&gt;
User-supplied backup location.
&lt;/stentry&gt;
&lt;/strow&gt;
&lt;/simpletable&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section&gt;
&lt;title&gt;Complex Syntax Example&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
The following syntax illustrates the use of keywords,
operators, and delimiters:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
&lt;synph&gt;
&lt;cmdname&gt;backup&lt;/cmdname&gt;
&lt;delim&gt;[&lt;/delim&gt;
&lt;option&gt;--full&lt;/option&gt;
&lt;oper&gt;|&lt;/oper&gt;
&lt;option&gt;--incremental&lt;/option&gt;
&lt;delim&gt;]&lt;/delim&gt;
&lt;kwd&gt;to&lt;/kwd&gt;
&lt;var&gt;destination&lt;/var&gt;
&lt;/synph&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section&gt;
&lt;title&gt;Example Command&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;codeblock outputclass="language-bash"&gt;
backup --full --compress /backups/prod
</codeblock>
    </section></refbody>
